<section class="seo-content" id="how-to-play" aria-labelledby="seo-heading">
  <div class="seo-inner">
    <h2 id="seo-heading">How to play Snake Game</h2>

    <p>
      Snake Game is the classic arcade game of growing a snake on a square board. You steer the snake
      toward the fruit; every fruit you eat adds a segment and scores points. The board never grows,
      so the longer you get, the harder every turn becomes — hit a wall or your own tail and the run
      is over.
    </p>

    <h3>Controls</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Steer:</strong> arrow keys or W / A / S / D.</li>
      <li><strong>Start, pause, resume:</strong> Space.</li>
      <li><strong>Pause:</strong> P (the game also pauses when the tab loses focus).</li>
      <li><strong>Restart:</strong> R, or Play again on the results screen.</li>
      <li><strong>On touch screens:</strong> swipe on the board or tap the direction pad.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Why this version</h3>
    <p>
      It runs instantly in your browser — no download, no login. Play on desktop, tablet, or phone,
      and your best score is saved on your device. You can pause mid-run, and when a run ends you can
      share your score.
    </p>

    <h3>A few tips</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Leave room to turn — don't trail too closely behind yourself.</li>
      <li>Stay near the middle early on, so you have space in every direction.</li>
      <li>Near the walls, plan two or three moves ahead instead of reacting.</li>
      <li>When it gets tense, pause and think.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

